.\" Man page for atlas session command
.\" Updated: July 2026
.TH SESSION 1 "July 2026" "atlas 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
atlas\-session \- session management for atlas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atlas session
\fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B atlas session
manages work sessions with automatic time tracking, context capture, and
ADHD-friendly features like celebration helpers and streak tracking.
.PP
Sessions are stored in \fI~/.atlas/sessions.json\fR (filesystem) or
\fI~/.atlas/atlas.db\fR (SQLite).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstart\fR [\fIproject\fR] [\fInote\fR]
Start a work session on the specified project. If no project is given,
uses the current directory. Optionally records an initial note.
.TP
\fBend\fR [\fInote\fR]
End the current active session. Records the end time and calculates
duration. Optionally records a completion note.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show the current active session (or "No active session").
.RS
Options:
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR
Output format: table, json, text (default: table).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON (alias for \-\-format json).
.RE
.TP
\fBexport\fR [\fIfile\fR]
Export sessions to iCal/ICS format for calendar apps.
.RS
Options:
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR \fIfile\fR
Output file path. Auto\-names if not given.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR
Export format: ical, ics, json (default: ical).
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fIdays\fR
Number of days to export (default: 30).
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIproject\fR
Filter by project name.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a session on the atlas project:
.RS
.nf
atlas session start atlas
.fi
.RE
.PP
End session with a note:
.RS
.nf
atlas session end "Completed man page docs"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show current session status:
.RS
.nf
atlas session status
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export last 7 days to iCal:
.RS
.nf
atlas session export \-\-days 7 sessions.ics
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.atlas/sessions.json
Session history (filesystem backend).
.TP
.I ~/.atlas/atlas.db
Session history (SQLite backend).
